IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bgg4-nouns`

-- bgg4-simplified: BGG 4. Kapitel, 6. Abschnitt, Vereinfachtes Verfahren (Art. 108 and 109).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively; nobody's point of view.
-- Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE (the text says yes), JUST FALSE (the text says no,
-- tagged FALSE-kind), NOTHING (not covered, tagged NOTHING-kind).  See bgg4-appealable for the key.
-- These two Articles say which judges decide in which cases.  Each is a power or a rule of
-- competence of the Court; the person is affected as the one whose appeal is decided in this way.
-- The terms the text leaves to the Court's judgment ("offensichtlich", "querulatorisch",
-- "rechtsmissbräuchlich", "von grundsätzlicher Bedeutung", "besonders bedeutender Fall") are
-- asked as plain facts.

§ `Art 108 Einzelrichter oder Einzelrichterin (single judge)`

-- src:117 | 1 Der Präsident oder die Präsidentin der Abteilung entscheidet im vereinfachten Verfahren über:
-- src:118 | a. Nichteintreten auf offensichtlich unzulässige Beschwerden;
@ref Art. 108(1)(a) BGG (src:117-118)
GIVEN `the appeal is obviously inadmissible` IS A BOOLEAN             -- offensichtlich unzulässig: an open-textured judgment, asked as a fact
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 108(1)(a) the president of the division decides in the simplified procedure on non-entry because the appeal is obviously inadmissible` MEANS
    IF `the appeal is obviously inadmissible`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): limb (a) names only "Nichteintreten auf offensichtlich unzulässige Beschwerden"

-- src:117 | 1 Der Präsident oder die Präsidentin der Abteilung entscheidet im vereinfachten Verfahren über:
-- src:119 | b. Nichteintreten auf Beschwerden, die offensichtlich keine hinreichende Begründung (Art. 42 Abs. 2) enthalten;
@ref Art. 108(1)(b) BGG (src:117) (src:119)
GIVEN `the appeal obviously contains no sufficient reasoning within the meaning of Art 42(2)` IS A BOOLEAN             -- offensichtlich keine hinreichende Begründung (Art. 42 Abs. 2): Art 42(2) is outside the sources
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 108(1)(b) the president of the division decides in the simplified procedure on non-entry because the appeal obviously lacks sufficient reasoning` MEANS
    IF `the appeal obviously contains no sufficient reasoning within the meaning of Art 42(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): limb (b) names only appeals that "offensichtlich keine hinreichende Begründung (Art. 42 Abs. 2) enthalten"; what Art 42(2) requires is outside the sources

-- src:117 | 1 Der Präsident oder die Präsidentin der Abteilung entscheidet im vereinfachten Verfahren über:
-- src:120 | c. Nichteintreten auf querulatorische oder rechtsmissbräuchliche Beschwerden.
@ref Art. 108(1)(c) BGG (src:117) (src:120)
GIVEN `the appeal is querulous or an abuse of rights` IS A BOOLEAN             -- querulatorisch oder rechtsmissbräuchlich: an open-textured judgment, asked as a fact
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 108(1)(c) the president of the division decides in the simplified procedure on non-entry because the appeal is querulous or an abuse of rights` MEANS
    IF `the appeal is querulous or an abuse of rights`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): limb (c) names only "querulatorische oder rechtsmissbräuchliche Beschwerden"

-- src:117 | 1 Der Präsident oder die Präsidentin der Abteilung entscheidet im vereinfachten Verfahren über:
-- src:118 | a. Nichteintreten auf offensichtlich unzulässige Beschwerden;
-- src:119 | b. Nichteintreten auf Beschwerden, die offensichtlich keine hinreichende Begründung (Art. 42 Abs. 2) enthalten;
-- src:120 | c. Nichteintreten auf querulatorische oder rechtsmissbräuchliche Beschwerden.
@ref Art. 108(1) BGG (src:117-120)
GIVEN `the appeal is obviously inadmissible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal obviously contains no sufficient reasoning within the meaning of Art 42(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is querulous or an abuse of rights` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 108(1) the president of the division decides in the simplified procedure on non-entry` MEANS
    IF     fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 108(1)(a) the president of the division decides in the simplified procedure on non-entry because the appeal is obviously inadmissible` `the appeal is obviously inadmissible`)
        OR fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 108(1)(b) the president of the division decides in the simplified procedure on non-entry because the appeal obviously lacks sufficient reasoning` `the appeal obviously contains no sufficient reasoning within the meaning of Art 42(2)`)
        OR fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 108(1)(c) the president of the division decides in the simplified procedure on non-entry because the appeal is querulous or an abuse of rights` `the appeal is querulous or an abuse of rights`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "entscheidet im vereinfachten Verfahren über: a. ...; b. ...; c. ..." names three matters; for an appeal of none of those kinds the paragraph says nothing (and says nothing of other judges)

-- src:121 | 2 Er oder sie kann einen anderen Richter oder eine andere Richterin damit betrauen.
@ref Art. 108(2) BGG (src:121)
GIVEN `the matter is one that paragraph 1 gives to the president of the division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge entrusted with the decision is another judge of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN        -- einen anderen Richter oder eine andere Richterin
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 108(2) the president of the division may entrust another judge with the decision` MEANS
    IF `the matter is one that paragraph 1 gives to the president of the division` AND `the judge entrusted with the decision is another judge of the Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a power ("kann ... betrauen") whose stated gate failed answers NOTHING, not a "may not" (ruling of 2026-11-12, limb 1; fork F17)

-- src:122 | 3 Die Begründung des Entscheids beschränkt sich auf eine kurze Angabe des Unzulässigkeitsgrundes.
@ref Art. 108(3) BGG (src:122)
GIVEN `the decision is one that paragraph 1 gives to the president of the division` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 108(3) the reasons of the decision are confined to a short statement of the ground of inadmissibility` MEANS
    IF `the decision is one that paragraph 1 gives to the president of the division`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Die Begründung des Entscheids beschränkt sich auf eine kurze Angabe des Unzulässigkeitsgrundes" speaks of the decision of paragraph 1

§ `Art 109 Dreierbesetzung (bench of three)`

-- First sentence.  The appeal is admissible "nur unter einer dieser Bedingungen" (a legal question of fundamental importance,
-- or a particularly important case), as Arts 74 and 83 to 85 of chapter 3 provide; bgg4-seams works that out from
-- chapter 3.  Where the appeal is admissible on either condition, the text's "oder" is read as: neither is present (fork F22).
-- src:125 | 1 Die Abteilungen entscheiden in Dreierbesetzung über Nichteintreten auf Beschwerden, bei denen sich keine Rechtsfrage von grundsätzlicher Bedeutung stellt oder kein besonders bedeutender Fall vorliegt, wenn die Beschwerde nur unter einer dieser Bedingungen zulässig ist (Art. 74 und 83–85). Artikel 58 Absatz 1 Buchstabe b findet keine Anwendung.
@ref Art. 109(1) BGG (first sentence) (src:125)
GIVEN condition IS A `Condition for admissibility in Art 109(1)`
      `a legal question of fundamental importance arises` IS A BOOLEAN       -- Rechtsfrage von grundsätzlicher Bedeutung
      `the case is a particularly important case` IS A BOOLEAN               -- besonders bedeutender Fall
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 109(1) the division decides in a bench of three on non-entry` MEANS
    CONSIDER condition
    WHEN `only if a legal question of fundamental importance arises` THEN
        IF NOT `a legal question of fundamental importance arises` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the competence reaches only an appeal in which "sich keine Rechtsfrage von grundsätzlicher Bedeutung stellt oder kein besonders bedeutender Fall vorliegt"
    WHEN `only if the case is a particularly important case` THEN
        IF NOT `the case is a particularly important case` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING             -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): see above
    WHEN `only if a legal question of fundamental importance arises or the case is a particularly important case` THEN
        IF (NOT `a legal question of fundamental importance arises`) AND (NOT `the case is a particularly important case`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): see above (fork F22)
    WHEN `on neither of these conditions` THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the competence reaches only an appeal that is "nur unter einer dieser Bedingungen zulässig"

-- src:125 | 1 Die Abteilungen entscheiden in Dreierbesetzung über Nichteintreten auf Beschwerden, bei denen sich keine Rechtsfrage von grundsätzlicher Bedeutung stellt oder kein besonders bedeutender Fall vorliegt, wenn die Beschwerde nur unter einer dieser Bedingungen zulässig ist (Art. 74 und 83–85). Artikel 58 Absatz 1 Buchstabe b findet keine Anwendung.
@ref Art. 109(1) BGG (second sentence) (src:125)
GIVEN condition IS A `Condition for admissibility in Art 109(1)`
      `a legal question of fundamental importance arises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is a particularly important case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 109(1) Art 58(1)(b) is applicable to the decision` MEANS
    IF `Art 109(1) the division decides in a bench of three on non-entry` condition `a legal question of fundamental importance arises` `the case is a particularly important case` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Artikel 58 Absatz 1 Buchstabe b findet keine Anwendung." (what Art 58(1)(b) provides is outside the sources)
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence follows the competence rule of the first sentence and is read with it; for any other decision it is silent

-- src:126 | 2 Sie entscheiden ebenfalls in Dreierbesetzung bei Einstimmigkeit über:
-- src:127 | a. Abweisung offensichtlich unbegründeter Beschwerden;
@ref Art. 109(2)(a) BGG (src:126-127)
GIVEN `the judges are unanimous` IS A BOOLEAN                              -- bei Einstimmigkeit
      `the appeal is obviously unfounded` IS A BOOLEAN                     -- offensichtlich unbegründet: an open-textured judgment, asked as a fact
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 109(2)(a) the division decides in a bench of three on dismissing the obviously unfounded appeal` MEANS
    IF `the judges are unanimous` AND `the appeal is obviously unfounded`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): limb (a) names only "Abweisung offensichtlich unbegründeter Beschwerden" "bei Einstimmigkeit"

-- src:126 | 2 Sie entscheiden ebenfalls in Dreierbesetzung bei Einstimmigkeit über:
-- src:128 | b. Gutheissung offensichtlich begründeter Beschwerden, insbesondere wenn der angefochtene Akt von der Rechtsprechung des Bundesgerichts abweicht und kein Anlass besteht, diese zu überprüfen.
@ref Art. 109(2)(b) BGG (src:126) (src:128)
GIVEN `the judges are unanimous` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is obviously well founded` IS A BOOLEAN                                                                               -- offensichtlich begründet: an open-textured judgment, asked as a fact
      `the challenged act departs from the case law of the Federal Supreme Court and there is no reason to review that case law` IS A BOOLEAN   -- insbesondere wenn der angefochtene Akt von der Rechtsprechung des Bundesgerichts abweicht und kein Anlass besteht, diese zu überprüfen
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 109(2)(b) the division decides in a bench of three on upholding the obviously well founded appeal` MEANS
    IF `the judges are unanimous` AND (`the appeal is obviously well founded` OR `the challenged act departs from the case law of the Federal Supreme Court and there is no reason to review that case law`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "insbesondere" gives the departure from case law as an example of an obviously well founded appeal and does not close the category; limb (b) names only "Gutheissung offensichtlich begründeter Beschwerden" "bei Einstimmigkeit"

-- src:126 | 2 Sie entscheiden ebenfalls in Dreierbesetzung bei Einstimmigkeit über:
-- src:127 | a. Abweisung offensichtlich unbegründeter Beschwerden;
-- src:128 | b. Gutheissung offensichtlich begründeter Beschwerden, insbesondere wenn der angefochtene Akt von der Rechtsprechung des Bundesgerichts abweicht und kein Anlass besteht, diese zu überprüfen.
@ref Art. 109(2) BGG (src:126-128)
GIVEN `the judges are unanimous` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is obviously unfounded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal is obviously well founded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the challenged act departs from the case law of the Federal Supreme Court and there is no reason to review that case law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 109(2) the division decides in a bench of three` MEANS
    IF     fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 109(2)(a) the division decides in a bench of three on dismissing the obviously unfounded appeal` `the judges are unanimous` `the appeal is obviously unfounded`)
        OR fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 109(2)(b) the division decides in a bench of three on upholding the obviously well founded appeal` `the judges are unanimous` `the appeal is obviously well founded` `the challenged act departs from the case law of the Federal Supreme Court and there is no reason to review that case law`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "ebenfalls in Dreierbesetzung bei Einstimmigkeit über: a. ...; b. ..." names two matters; for any other the paragraph says nothing

-- src:129 | 3 Der Entscheid wird summarisch begründet. Es kann ganz oder teilweise auf den angefochtenen Entscheid verwiesen werden.
@ref Art. 109(3) BGG (first sentence) (src:129)
GIVEN `the decision is one that paragraph 1 or 2 gives to a bench of three` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 109(3) the decision is given summary reasons` MEANS
    IF `the decision is one that paragraph 1 or 2 gives to a bench of three`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Der Entscheid wird summarisch begründet" speaks of the decisions of paragraphs 1 and 2

-- src:129 | 3 Der Entscheid wird summarisch begründet. Es kann ganz oder teilweise auf den angefochtenen Entscheid verwiesen werden.
@ref Art. 109(3) BGG (second sentence) (src:129)
GIVEN `the decision is one that paragraph 1 or 2 gives to a bench of three` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 109(3) the reasons may refer wholly or in part to the challenged decision` MEANS
    IF `the decision is one that paragraph 1 or 2 gives to a bench of three`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a permission ("Es kann ... verwiesen werden") for the decisions of paragraphs 1 and 2; for any other decision the sentence says nothing (ruling of 2026-11-12, limb 1; fork F17)
